 "about": "Lobbying filed by or for cultural spaces in this atlas, as the client, from public registers. Built 17 Nov 2026 by matching all 1,727 spaces against the US Lobbying Disclosure Act database (lda.gov API, every filing since 1999) and the EU Transparency Register export of 16 Nov 2026. Each match was checked by hand; namesakes were removed (Triple Canopy the defence contractor, Recess the CBD drinks company, the Fresno Metropolitan Museum). US amounts are what each report states: an outside firm's income from the space, or the space's own expenses when it files itself (its own figure already includes the firms it paid, so the two are not added). A report under $5,000 states no amount and counts as $0. 2026 holds the quarters filed so far. EU entries in the public or NGO categories declare a total budget, not a lobbying cost. Not covered: state and city lobbying registers, the UK, Ireland, Scotland and Canada.",
